# Two-system mining loop for overmind. Overrides data/scripts/idle_mine.smolt
# (data/agents/<id>/scripts wins in ScriptSearchPaths).
#
# Why not just mine at home: the_anvil is picked over for ore, and this agent was
# logging "Resources depleted" every other pass. hd_20794 has NO STATION, which is
# exactly why its rock is untouched — 100,102 remaining at richness 56, the highest richness within one jump. Nobody mines where they cannot dock.
#
# Home stays the_anvil because its fuel desk is MEASURED (station_fuel_prices).
# The nearer low-security systems with their own station — alzirr, gsc_0034,
# tiaki, silvermark — have never had a fuel reading, and an unverified desk in
# lawless space is how an agent strands.
#
# refuel is LAST so the tank is full before the next pass's outbound jump.
# loop -f tolerates "Resources depleted" and exits early on cargo_full, which
# the server reports as a GoalReachedError.
#
# get_system after EVERY jump is load-bearing, not decoration. $ASTEROID_BELT$
# and $STATION$ resolve against the client's cached POI list, which still holds
# the PREVIOUS system's POIs immediately after a jump. Without the refresh,
# miner-10 jumped to frostfeld and then tried to travel to "Ironhearth Fields",
# the belt it had just left, and the pass died there (observed 2026-08-21).
# get_system is an info query: no tick cost.
#
# The belt is named LITERALLY, not via $ASTEROID_BELT$. HD 20794 has two, and
# FindMiningLocation returns the FIRST one in the system's POI list with no
# richness ranking — which is hd_20794_belt, the poor one (~24k across all
# resources). This agent ran at a 50%% depleted rate there while every other
# miner sat at 100%%. hd_20794_forge_vein holds 62,283 copper_ore + 12,875
# iron_ore. Any multi-belt system needs the POI named outright.
jump hd_20794
get_system
travel hd_20794_forge_vein
loop -f 100 mine
jump the_anvil
get_system
travel $STATION$
dock
deposit_all
refuel
